5) Kubernetes created a Deployment named nginx using the NGINX container image.
-->  kubectl create deployment nginx --image nginx
OP : deployment.apps/nginx created
explain: Break the command into pieces:
kubectl    create    deployment    nginx    --image nginx
  │          │           │           │           │
  │          │           │           │           └── Container image
  │          │           │           └── Deployment name
  │          │           └── Resource type
  │          └── Action
  └── Kubernetes command-line tool
  
  What did Kubernetes actually create?
  explain : 
  Deployment
     │
     │ creates/manages
     ▼
 ReplicaSet
     │
     │ creates/manages
     ▼
    Pod
     │
     │ runs
     ▼
 Container
     │
     ▼
   NGINX
So after your command, Kubernetes has approximately:
Deployment: nginx
       │
       ▼
ReplicaSet: nginx-xxxxxxxx
       │
       ▼
Pod: nginx-xxxxxxxx-xxxxx
       │
       ▼
NGINX container
By default, your Deployment has 1 replica.

